  <title>Products</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Products</gui></guiseq>, or
  <gui>Products</gui> in the menu of an invoice or purchase order, lists the
  products. Choose which to show above the list: <gui>Sellable</gui>,
  <gui>Purchasable</gui>, <gui>Manufactured</gui>, <gui>Job</gui>, <gui>Non
  stock</gui>, <gui>All</gui> or <gui>Deleted</gui>. Type in <gui>Search
  product name</gui> to narrow the list. When a product is changed elsewhere,
  <gui>Refresh</gui> appears; click it to reload the list.</p>

  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>New</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>N</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Adds a product; see <link xref="product_edit_main"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Edit</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>E</key></keyseq>),
    or double click</title>
    <p>Changes the selected product.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Order numbers</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>O</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Each vendor's number for the product; see <link
    xref="#order_numbers"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Product location</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>L</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Where it is kept; see <link xref="#location"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Product hub</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>H</key></keyseq>)</title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="product_hub"/>.</p></item>
  </terms>
  <p>The same actions are in the right click menu of the list. The window menu
  has <gui>Print label</gui> (see <link xref="product_print_label"/>),
  <gui>Report hub</gui> to export the list (see <link xref="report_hub"/>),
  and <gui>Save window layout</gui>, which remembers the window's size and
  column widths on this computer. <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Q</key></keyseq>
  closes the window. Drag a product onto an invoice or purchase order to add
  it there.</p>

  <section id="order_numbers">
  <title>Order numbers</title>
  <p>A product can be bought from several vendors, each with its own order
  number. Click <gui>New row</gui>, choose the <gui>Vendor</gui> and type their
  <gui>Order number</gui>, the <gui>Barcode</gui> on their package, and any
  <gui>Buy qty</gui> and <gui>Price</gui>. The <gui>Buy qty</gui> can be a sum
  such as <input>2x12</input>; see <link xref="qty_arithmetic"/>.
  <gui>Delete row</gui> removes the
  selected one. <gui>Save</gui> keeps the changes; <gui>Cancel</gui> discards
  them. Only one person can change a product's order numbers at a time.</p>
  <p>A purchase order fills in the order number for its vendor, and a
  number changed on a purchase order can be saved back here; see <link
  xref="purchase_order#order_number"/>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="location">
  <title>Product location</title>
  <p>Choose the <gui>Location</gui> and fill in where the product is kept
  there: <gui>Aisle</gui>, <gui>Rack</gui>, <gui>Cart</gui>, <gui>Shelf</gui>,
  <gui>Cabinet</gui>, <gui>Drawer</gui> and <gui>Bin</gui>. Click
  <gui>Save</gui>, or press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>S</key></keyseq>.
  The location prints on shelf labels. To see every product's location, use
  <link xref="product_location"/>.</p>
  </section>

